; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Silly Sentence Machine
; CATEGORY: Words & Text
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     random, pick, sentence, grammar, label
; SUMMARY:  Builds random funny sentences from lists of nouns, verbs and adjectives and writes them across the screen in color.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Every sentence is made from the same recipe:
;     the  ADJECTIVE  NOUN  VERB  the  ADJECTIVE  NOUN  PLACE
;   but each part is picked at random, so you get things like
;     "the sleepy dragon tickled the purple sandwich under the bed"
;   Eight sentences are printed and drawn on the screen, each in its
;   own color.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run as many times as you like; it is different every time.
;   Type   print silly   in the command center for one more sentence.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * PICK chooses a random item from a list
;   * SENTENCE glues words and lists together into one list
;   * small procedures, each building one part of the sentence
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add your own words to the lists (your friends' names, your pets)
;   * Add an ADVERB list (quickly, loudly) and put it after the verb
;   * Change "the" to "a" in SOMEBODY, then make it say "an" before
;     words that start with a vowel (an ancient wizard)
; ============================================================

make "adjectives [sleepy purple giant tiny grumpy sparkly invisible ~
  wobbly hungry polite ancient fluffy noisy secret]
make "nouns [dragon sandwich robot teacher penguin pirate cupcake ~
  wizard turtle banana dinosaur astronaut kitten volcano]
make "verbs [tickled chased hugged painted juggled [sang to] ~
  borrowed squashed interviewed rescued]
make "places [[under the bed] [on the moon] [at the library] ~
  [inside a teapot] [during lunch] [in the bathtub] [at midnight] ~
  [behind the school]]

; Each helper outputs a small piece. Splitting the work up like this
; makes it easy to change one part of the recipe.
to somebody
  output (sentence "the pick :adjectives pick :nouns)
end

to silly
  output (sentence somebody pick :verbs somebody pick :places)
end

; Write one sentence on the turtle screen at height :y.
to show.line :y :sent :color
  penup setxy -380 :y
  setpencolor :color
  label :sent
end

to main
  clearscreen hideturtle setbackground [25 25 50]
  localmake "colors [[255 120 120] [255 200 90] [255 255 120] ~
    [140 240 140] [120 220 255] [170 150 255] [255 150 230] [230 230 230]]
  penup setxy -120 240 setpencolor 7 setlabelheight 28
  label [Silly Sentences]
  setlabelheight 16
  for [i 1 8] [
    localmake "s silly
    print :s
    show.line 180 - 52 * :i :s item :i :colors
  ]
end

main
